--   Test Description
--   
--   This test ensures that the GEM does not burst across a 1K AHB boundary.
--   This test is setup for maximum 4-beat bursts with 32/64/128-bit words.
--   
--   Functional Coverage
--   * Tests the 1K boundary detection within the gem_ahb module for 
--     4-beat bursts
--   
--   Detailed Test Description
--   
-- 1. Set wait states for test
-- 2. Initialise for 100M, 32 bit mode and enable all interrupts
-- 3. In 32 bit mode transmit four frames each of 48 bytes of DMA data, and
--    enable padding/CRC appending (i.e. 64 bytes are transmitted).
--    In 32-bit mode, 48 bytes will take 3 bursts of four 32-bit words to read.
--    Move the 1k boundary onto each of the four words of the second burst 
--    over the four frames. (e.g 1k boundary is on fourth word of second burst
--    in the first frame, third word of second burst in second frame, etc.)
--    Verify that all bursts other than the second burst of all frames are
--    signalled as an INCR4 AHB burst on the HBURST signal. Verify that bursts
--    which do cross a 1k boundary are signalled as single accesses.
-- 4. In 64 bit mode transmit four frames each of 96 bytes of DMA data, and
--    disable padding/CRC appending.
--    In 64-bit mode, 96 bytes will take 3 bursts of four 64-bit words to read.
--    Move the 1k boundary onto each of the four words of the second burst 
--    over the four frames. (e.g 1k boundary is on fourth word of second burst
--    in the first frame, third word of second burst in second frame, etc.)
--    Verify that all bursts other than the second burst of all frames are
--    signalled as an INCR4 AHB burst on the HBURST signal. Verify that bursts
--    which do cross a 1k boundary are signalled as single accesses.
-- 5. In 128 bit mode transmit four frames each of 192 bytes of DMA data, and
--    disable padding/CRC appending.
--    In 128-bit mode, 192 bytes will take 3 bursts of four 128-bit words to
--    read. Move the 1k boundary onto each of the four words of the second burst
--    over the four frames. (e.g 1k boundary is on fourth word of second burst
--    in the first frame, third word of second burst in second frame, etc.)
--    Verify that all bursts other than the second burst of all frames are
--    signalled as an INCR4 AHB burst on the HBURST signal. Verify that bursts
--    which do cross a 1k boundary are signalled as single accesses.
-- 6. In 32 bit mode transmit four frames each of 32 bytes of DMA data, and
--    enable padding/CRC appending (i.e. 64 bytes are transmitted).
--    In 32-bit mode, 32 bytes will take 2 bursts of four 32-bit words to read.
--    Move the 1k boundary onto each of the four words of the first burst 
--    over the four frames. (e.g 1k boundary is on fourth word of first burst
--    in the first frame, third word of first burst in second frame, etc.)
--    Verify that all bursts other than the first burst of all frames are
--    signalled as an INCR4 AHB burst on the HBURST signal. Verify that bursts
--    which do cross a 1k boundary are signalled as single accesses.
-- 7. Check the statistics to ensure the above operations were handled correctly
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------


-- *****************************************************************************
-- 1. Set wait states for test
-- *****************************************************************************
